Commit message format for this repo. Keep it short; details belong in the body.

Subject line, imperative mood, under 72 characters, no trailing period.
Optional prefix when it names a layer or area, matching what is already
here: "15-ours: ", "README: ", "docs: ", "mesa3d: ".

    <subject>

Body. Quote the error verbatim first when there is one, indented two
spaces so it reads as pasted output. Then say what the cause was and
what changed. Wrap at 72. End with the verification, as a count:

    <n> patches, 0 conflicts.

Example:

    mesa3d: call ld.lld by absolute path

      external/mesa3d/.../build.sh: ...: ld.lld: not found

    Soong runs the linker from PATH, and Arch ships it as ld.lld with no
    ld.lld alias in the build environment. Use the absolute path.

    194 patches, 0 conflicts.

Two things not to do:

  - Do not add Conventional Commits prefixes such as "fix:" or
    "chore:". Only 4 of the 31 existing commits use one, and they read as
    imported from elsewhere.
  - Do not leave the body empty. Every commit that diagnosed a build
    failure records the error it was fixing; that is the part worth
    reading later.